            "review_title": "Review at Tien Phat Dim Sum Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Wenglairene\nSingapore, Singapore79 contributions\n0\nGood dim sum and value for money\nJul 2019 • Couples\nDon't be fooled by the unassuming look of the restaurant. It is non-air conditioned downstairs, but there are air conditioned tables upstairs. So if you can't stand the heat, you can opt for the air conditioned tables, if you are early and lucky enough to find a table. We went there during an off peak time (weekday 11.30 a.m.) The place was not packed, but there were quite a number of tables occupied. We ordered a shrimp noodle which was very tasty and came with 4 large prawns. We also ordered 3 other dim sum dishes - har gao, cheong fun with shrimp and shrimp wrapped in beancurd. The shrimps were medium to large size and the dim sum was really nice. It could be equivalent to the dim sum that I eat in popular fine dining restaurants back here in Singapore. Together with a pot of tea, the entire bill only came up to less than 300,000 VND, which is pretty ok given the food quality. Definitely would come again.\nRead more\nWritten July 15, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
