            "review_text": "robynemmalee\nSeoul, South Korea23 contributions\n0\nDelicious dim sum\nJul 2018 • Couples\nWe arrived mid morning on a Sunday, perhaps the busiest time? We waited about 10 mins for a table after putting our names on the list. They gave us cold tea while we waited. We got a table on a narrow terrace on the 4th floor. Be prepared for a very busy, cramped and hectic environment. It took a while for the table to be cleaned from the previous diners and the food took about 15 mins to arrive. We ordered a variety of typical dim sum and each dish was executed extremely well. It was on par with London China town. The tea was free too. It seemed that noodle soups were a specialty there as most of the locals seemed to be having a noodle soup each and a few dim sum to share. \n\nTo summarise, I would say that the food is excellent and the prices are competitive but be prepared to wait for a table and for food. The tables are rammed close together and the environment is quite hectic. Although the staff were rushing around and took a while to serve us, they they were very polite and just seemed overwhelmed with the quantity of customers. \n\nOpening times: 6am - 12.30pm (morning only!)\nRead more\nWritten July 29, 2018",
